829-
830-- Accepted doctrine already uses thin milestone plans, dispatch-time model routing, bounded gate retries, delta-context validation, and fresh-context verification. Instruction hygiene is a follow-on rightsizing/evaluation effort, not permission to remove gates or reopen model policy. [Task 1]
831-- Before editing instruction artifacts, consult `docs/ARTIFACT-UPSTREAM-REGISTRY.md`; do not patch deployed/mirrored copies. Check MeatySkills ownership for `delegation-router`, `model-playbook`, and dynamic workflow scripts. Exclude `.agents/`, `.claude/worktrees/`, and `docs/enablement/**/artifacts/` from first-wave audits. [Task 1]
832:- Evaluate 18–24 sanitized cases with deterministic oracles, isolated-worktree baseline/candidate runs, one change family per branch, repeated trials, and correctness/scope/safety-gate fidelity/unsupported-completion/tokens/turns/tool-call metrics. [Task 1]
833-- Accept a candidate only with no safety, approval, provenance, validation, duplicate-write, or unsupported-completion regression; require equal-or-better correctness/scope plus measured efficiency improvement. Any safety failure, unauthorized write, or incorrect completion claim is a stop condition. Static scores are triage, never merge authority. [Task 1]
834-- Reporails advertises `npx @reporails/cli check` and 120+ rules, but its determinism and data boundary were not established. Use it only as a sanitized, disposable comparison after supplier/privacy review. [Task 1]
