# Corrected visual baseline

## Why rendered references

The earlier generated screens changed content and behavior between frames. This pack instead includes screenshots of one working HTML implementation. They share one typography/color/layout system and the same thread/evidence records. These are the normative visual references for **layout and visible state**, subject to the specific missing-artwork boundary below.

The technical diagrams shown are explicitly labeled HTML schematics because the eight latest canonical PNG files are unavailable here. They are not new approved technical figures and must not replace those images in production. The hero uses the actual supplied workshop illustration. The author avatar is a monogram, not a generated portrait.

## Screen atlas

| Screen | View / purpose |
|---|---|
| 01 | Essay entry: hero, title, flow author and Executive Signal |
| 02 | Initial scroll: thread incident and sticky companion, no entry cards |
| 03 | Partial-width artifact composition, taxonomy and authored ContextualNote |
| 04 | Inline Deployment + companion; manual state controls |
| 05 | Thread Focus: Use, artifact card and six-beat overview only |
| 06 | Evidence Focus: expanded method summary, collapsed other records, guide/index |
| 07 | Figure Viewer: exact scene context, caption and long description |
| 08 | Managed variation: explicitly illustrative project decisions |
| 09 | Essay ending: actual reading path, no invented next essay |
| 10–13 | Mobile entry, Contents sheet, full-screen Thread and Evidence Focus |
| Additional | All remaining thread scenes; held/collapsed dock and direct standalone details |

Use the gallery `index.html` to browse the actual files. Component-label variants are review-only; labels must not ship in production.

## Visual tokens

Dark navy ground, slightly raised blue-gray panels, bone/light-blue type, one violet navigation accent, cyan links/structure, amber for clearly labeled uncertainty. Green is not a general approval/success decoration. Static subtle gradients are appropriate; a giant planet, stars or parallax behind text are not required.

Use serif display headings, system/site sans for UI, a comfortable reading measure and larger pane-width figure surfaces. Distinguish ordinary paragraphs from actual cards. Do not put a border around every content block.

## Prompt guide for any later generative polish pass

Generated comps are optional atmosphere studies, not factual/UI contract authority. Prefer rendering from the implementation when a state needs exact labels.

### Global locked constraints

Use the chosen dark editorial design and the exact v2 mode. Do not add components not listed for that mode. Do not invent evidence, controls, quotes, dates, metrics, sources, artifact versions, routes or publication claims. Do not regenerate an author portrait. Use NM or the actual approved portrait. Keep the domain `nickmiethe.com`. If canonical art is absent, show a clearly labeled reserved figure area rather than improvising its content.

### Essay section composition

Render a scrolled essay section titled “What counts as an artifact.” A numbered left rule marks the active section in violet. Prose and a compact illustrative capability card share only the primary pane. Beneath is a full-primary-pane semantic taxonomy table with Instruction, Tool, Context, Governance, Execution, Evidence. The right rail contains ReadingCompanion plus one authored ContextualNote: “The runtime executes. An artifact shapes its behavior.” No author or Executive Signal at this scroll location.

### Thread Focus composition

Render a near-full-screen focused reading surface. Top bar: “Back to essay,” “Reading place saved,” “Copy link,” Close. Main: “03 / 06 — Use,” “Present in a file does not mean followed in a run,” explicit “Conceptual branch,” figure area and evidence limit. Right rail: **only** RunningExampleCard for `task-completion-validator` and ThreadOverview with Incident, Deployment, Use, Drift, Detection, Outcome. No article TOC, author bio, Executive Signal or chatbot. Do not turn the guard instruction into a gateway.

### Evidence Focus composition

Render an evidence-focused reading surface using the same visual tokens. One expanded “Deployed-copy drift” method summary, three collapsed related summaries and a proposed run-record item. Show support and limitations side by side. State “Primary capture not included” where necessary. No simulated terminal output, signing implementation, measurement chart or fake commit. Right rail: EvidenceGuide and ReceiptIndex only.

### Mobile composition

Show the responsive article with real website navigation, cropped editorial hero, large serif title and small Contents action. Alternate state: touch-sized Contents sheet or full-screen Thread Focus with persistent Back to essay. No installed-app tab bar, AI thread, robot assistant or fabricated service routes.

## Publication boundary

Visual approval cannot clear a factual claim. The final manuscript and technical image pixels require their own review. A beautiful image with invented evidence remains rejected.
